---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { COMPANY, CONTACT } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How we collect, use and protect your data when you use our website, submit an inquiry or subscribe to our newsletter."
  path="/privacy-policy/"
>
  <Section title="Privacy Policy">
    <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 [&_h2]:mt-8 [&_h2]:text-lg [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:text-slate-900">
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Last updated: September 2026</p>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-xs text-amber-800">
        <strong>Note:</strong> This is a technical placeholder. Have the final text
        reviewed by a legal professional before launch, especially for EU visitors
        (GDPR) and other regulated markets.
      </div>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        The controller of the personal data described in this policy is {COMPANY.legalName}.
        You can reach us about privacy matters at
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`} class="text-brand-700 underline">{CONTACT.email}</a>.
        TODO: add the registered address and, where required, an EU/UK representative.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Data we collect</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
        <li><strong>Inquiry data</strong>: name, company, country, email, phone/WhatsApp, product interest, quantity and message — provided by you when submitting the inquiry form.</li>
        <li><strong>Chat data</strong>: the messages you exchange with the AI sales assistant, the products it recommended to you, and — if you choose to provide them — your email address, WhatsApp number, name, company and country. The conversation is stored in your browser session and sent to us only when you submit contact details; nothing is stored on our servers without it.</li>
        <li><strong>Newsletter data</strong>: email address — provided only with your explicit marketing consent.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics data</strong>: anonymized usage statistics (Google Analytics 4), loaded only after you consent via the cookie banner. Chat interactions are measured as aggregate events only; the content of your messages, your email address and your phone number are never sent to analytics.</li>
        <li><strong>Attribution data</strong>: UTM parameters and referring page, used solely to understand which channel your inquiry came from.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. How we use your data</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
        <li>Inquiry data is used to respond to your request and prepare quotations.</li>
        <li>Chat messages are used to understand your requirement, recommend a product and let our sales team follow up on the contact details you provide.</li>
        <li>Newsletter data is used to send marketing emails you explicitly opted in to. You can unsubscribe at any time.</li>
        <li>Submitting an inquiry or a chat lead does <strong>not</strong> subscribe you to marketing emails.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Cookies and consent</h2>
      <p>
        Marketing and analytics cookies are only set after you click "Accept all"
        in the consent banner. "Necessary only" keeps them disabled. You can change
        your choice at any time by clearing site data in your browser.
        The chat widget does not set cookies: the conversation is kept in your
        browser's session storage and is discarded when you close the tab.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Third-party processors</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
        <li>Google Analytics (statistics, consent-based)</li>
        <li>Cloudflare (hosting, CDN, bot protection, and the Turnstile challenge that protects our forms and chat)</li>
        <li>Resend (transactional email delivery)</li>
        <li>An AI language-model provider (processing of chat messages in order to draft the assistant's replies)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>International transfers.</strong> These providers may process data on
        servers outside your country, including outside the EEA. Where required, the
        transfer is covered by appropriate safeguards such as the Standard
        Contractual Clauses.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>What the AI provider receives.</strong> Only the text needed to draft a
        reply: your message and the product information being discussed. Email
        addresses and phone numbers you enter in the chat are detected in your
        browser and sent straight to our own lead pipeline — they are not sent to the
        AI provider, and message history passed to the model is screened for contact
        details before it leaves our server.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You may request access, correction or deletion of your personal data at any
        time by emailing
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`} class="text-brand-700 underline">{CONTACT.email}</a>.
        TODO: add any market-specific rights text (GDPR Art. 15–21, etc.) and an
        EU/UK representative where one is required.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        Inquiry data and chat leads are retained as long as needed to handle your
        request and for legitimate business record-keeping. Chat conversations that
        were never submitted to us as a lead are not retained on our side at all —
        they exist only in the session storage of your own browser.
        TODO: confirm the retention period (e.g. 24 months) with the legal reviewer.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
